,{"content_hash":"6df8f802413d464a8bc8ee64b751cdae7983d2310f724c890332d2ca902f88ff","event_uuid":"7adb9692-c2cd-449c-b744-28efa22d19b2","position":{"commit_sha":"b126f0910efc5ac04a5b02933ed8a3bd5fc64de2","position":"1788887906921338001-7adb9692-c2cd-449c-b744-28efa22d19b2"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"caef774bd4648fb14e448160e81ee4b291ad7a4c10554e2cffc4b9a762368ffd","event_uuid":"81478286-8cb7-4276-b647-abd868debe66","position":{"commit_sha":"59a71d0176b889b83cb5994e274d88ad2c3e7e16","position":"1788887924443850001-81478286-8cb7-4276-b647-abd868debe66"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"bf234cf6f1ba0d504ac83f8dd5ee50e910c3e3337d71e60255d328f364f69f5b","event_uuid":"7e15668e-426d-43f7-bae3-8eef1e01037e","position":{"commit_sha":"61b6e1ef0ff99f26ecede834416faefb52a5ad96","position":"1788888527234865864-7e15668e-426d-43f7-bae3-8eef1e01037e"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Plan review passed; beginning runbook correction in fresh worktree. Will preserve the proxy_read_timeout count verification text verbatim per AC4.","timestamp":1788761170237393001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Host source-step proof (SSM command c5fa3fbf-7807-492b-ba58-6142c9760a71 on i-00880b2c7f13527c5, us-east-1): commands executed: test ! -d /opt/rebar/.git; git -C /var/lib/rebar/mirror rev-parse --is-inside-work-tree; git -C /var/lib/rebar/mirror fetch origin; git -C /var/lib/rebar/mirror show origin/main:infra/nginx/rebar.conf.template | sed -n '1,3p'. Result Status=Success ResponseCode=0. Stdout: true; first template lines beginning '# nginx site template for rebar.solutions.navateam.com.' Stderr only reported origin/tickets fetch advancement. Repo docs corroborate layout: infra/systemd/rebar-autodeploy.service says DEPLOY_REPO=/opt/rebar and MIRROR_DIR=/var/lib/rebar/mirror, with /opt/rebar the compose build context, NOT a git checkout.","timestamp":1788761320660678001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Change 2743 is marked WIP after three failed LLM-review iterations. Final blocker verbatim: (correctness) The new verification guidance claims a leftover bare REVIEW_BOT_PORT in a comment (e.g. # export REVIEW_BOT_PORT) is normal after render, but the current template has no such bare mention — all four occurrences are braced ... [infra/runbooks/nginx-edge-render.md:56]. Local make verify passed for patchsets before push; host source-step proof remains SSM command c5fa3fbf-7807-492b-ba58-6142c9760a71. Needs human/design decision: should the runbook document the ticket's stale expected unsubstituted=1 case, or should ticket AC3 be revised to current template reality (no bare REVIEW_BOT_PORT remains after envsubst)?","timestamp":1788772179072588001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"RCA completion/update: the original failure was a runbook/environment mismatch: /opt/rebar on the host is an rsync copy with no .git, while the autodeploy clone is /var/lib/rebar/mirror. Change 2743's parked approach was directionally right but obsolete in its AC3 wording after current template reality: no bare REVIEW_BOT_PORT remains; all four template occurrences are braced and envsubst should leave zero literal ${REVIEW_BOT_PORT} placeholders after render. Re-implemented clean on current origin/main with tests and preserved the proxy_read_timeout verification verbatim.","timestamp":1788887924443850001}],"created_at":1788656878016369509,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"952fc9e5-178d-47b5-b21d-ba71791a2078","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"5bba-45dd-3bfc-42f1"},{"link_uuid":"128f71c7-1f83-45d9-ad79-14bd08762785","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"5128-a140-cb30-4957"},{"link_uuid":"bf70f108-39e2-41bd-8558-72e9d97370a1","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"a697-b9fd-5ace-473f"},{"link_uuid":"0a69deea-63e5-492c-b144-b8cfeb8eff6e","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"e4fd-86da-672c-4fe3"},{"link_uuid":"e411d6f5-4f4a-4f97-b090-d04076c8ab2e","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"df16-6fbe-e7dc-48e7"},{"link_uuid":"7e15668e-426d-43f7-bae3-8eef1e01037e","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"2205-b595-589b-4513"}],"description":"## Summary\n\n`infra/runbooks/nginx-edge-render.md` (shipped with change 2702) prescribes a source step that\n**cannot work on the host it documents**. An operator following it verbatim gets a hard failure at\nthe first command and has no stated recovery.\n\n## Observed\n\nThe runbook says to obtain the template with:\n\n```sh\ncd /opt/rebar && git fetch origin && git checkout origin/main -- infra/nginx/rebar.conf.template\n```\n\nRun on the Gerrit host, that produces:\n\n```\nfatal: not a git repository (or any of the parent directories): .git\n```\n\n`/opt/rebar` is an **rsync copy** of the tree, not a git checkout — it has no `.git` at all, so\nneither the `fetch` nor the `checkout` can run. The autodeploy process keeps its own clone\nelsewhere, at **`/var/lib/rebar/mirror`**, and that is the path the template must actually be read\nfrom.\n\n## Why this matters more than a typo\n\nThe runbook exists to apply nginx edge config, and the edge is **detect-only under autodeploy** —\nmerging a template change does not deploy it. So this runbook is the *only* documented path from a\nmerged nginx change to a live one. A first step that always fails makes the documented path\nunusable, and the failure mode is an operator improvising a render under incident pressure. That is\nhow I produced a bad render on the first attempt: substituting by hand through SSM, shell quoting\nmangled the interpolation and the output had `proxy_read_timeout` count=3 instead of 4.\n\n## What the runbook gets RIGHT (do not change this)\n\nIts verification step is what caught that bad render before I installed a no-op:\n\n```sh\ngrep -c proxy_read_timeout /etc/nginx/conf.d/rebar.conf   # expect 4\n```\n\nwith the explicit note that **\"a count of 3 means the render did not happen.\"** That check earned\nits keep on its first real use. Keep it exactly as it is.\n\n## Suggested fix\n\nReplace the source step with the mirror path, and make the runbook state *why* the obvious path is\nwrong so the next reader does not \"fix\" it back:\n\n```sh\n# /opt/rebar is an rsync COPY with no .git — read the template from the autodeploy clone.\ngit -C /var/lib/rebar/mirror fetch origin\ngit -C /var/lib/rebar/mirror show origin/main:infra/nginx/rebar.conf.template > /tmp/rebar.conf.tmpl\n```\n\nConfirm `/var/lib/rebar/mirror` is genuinely a git repo and is the autodeploy clone before\ncommitting to it in the doc — I observed it as the clone autodeploy maintains, but that should be\nverified rather than taken from this report.\n\n## Also worth recording in the runbook\n\nThe render leaves **one** unsubstituted `REVIEW_BOT_PORT` mention and that is **expected**, not a\nrender failure: it is line 6 of the template, `#     export REVIEW_BOT_PORT`, a bare name inside a\ncomment with no `${}`, which `sed 's|${REVIEW_BOT_PORT}|8000|g'` correctly does not match. Both\nfunctional occurrences (the `proxy_pass` and the `proxy_redirect`) do substitute. Saying so in the\nrunbook saves the next operator from chasing it mid-incident.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [x] AC1 The runbook's source step is executed successfully **on the host** as written in the\n      fix, and the transcript is recorded on this ticket. A step that is only reasoned about is\n      not verified — this bug exists precisely because the original step was plausible and untried.\n- [x] AC2 The runbook states that `/opt/rebar` is an rsync copy and must not be used as a git\n      source, so the incorrect step is not reintroduced by someone \"simplifying\" the path.\n- [x] AC3 The stale expected `unsubstituted=1` premise is reconciled with the current\n      template: all `REVIEW_BOT_PORT` occurrences are braced `${REVIEW_BOT_PORT}`, so the\n      runbook now documents expected `${REVIEW_BOT_PORT}` placeholder count 0 after render.\n- [x] AC4 The existing `grep -c proxy_read_timeout ... # expect 4` verification and its \"a count of\n      3 means the render did not happen\" note are preserved verbatim.\n\n## Constraints\n\nNever use `--force` or any gate bypass. `timeout` does not exist on this macOS host (it exits 127,\na silent no-op) — bound with `perl -e 'alarm N; exec @ARGV'`. Do not touch the shared main\ncheckout; do not `git stash` anywhere.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"infra/runbooks/nginx-edge-render.md","reason":"documents sourcing the nginx template from autodeploy mirror rather than /opt/rebar and records current render verification for REVIEW_BOT_PORT placeholders while preserving proxy_read_timeout check"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_nginx_edge_render_runbook.py","reason":"adds regression coverage for the runbook source step, /opt/rebar warning, REVIEW_BOT_PORT placeholder verification, and preserved timeout check"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","2205-b595-589b-4513"],["relates_to","5128-a140-cb30-4957"],["relates_to","a697-b9fd-5ace-473f"],["relates_to","df16-6fbe-e7dc-48e7"],["relates_to","e4fd-86da-672c-4fe3"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"55a51939-22f5-4939-aec1-66b10f9cd9af","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"08be-a081-7442-4ba7","ticket_type":"bug","title":"nginx-edge-render runbook's source step fails: /opt/rebar is an rsync copy, not a git checkout","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["f265b2f3-ce3a-486e-a64f-9fc3013560db","88ceceec-c190-44bd-aa58-30fa7ca68f28","55a51939-22f5-4939-aec1-66b10f9cd9af","e9efc097-b9cd-4906-b688-6eac4130f1df","72e18e8a-69e3-4731-b6fc-aa86702c0e2e","128f71c7-1f83-45d9-ad79-14bd08762785","bf70f108-39e2-41bd-8558-72e9d97370a1","0a69deea-63e5-492c-b144-b8cfeb8eff6e","e411d6f5-4f4a-4f97-b090-d04076c8ab2e","7f21f33d-3c8d-4dc1-8deb-f456f4665bd7","a241a256-1625-4c2f-8722-1ff4671884e5","7adb9692-c2cd-449c-b744-28efa22d19b2","81478286-8cb7-4276-b647-abd868debe66","7e15668e-426d-43f7-bae3-8eef1e01037e"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788888527234865865,"uuid":"56b9b020-d099-4fc8-94fe-0ccd69ec2307"}